00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:42.720
Your being an automated doll
has nothing to do with my instinct!

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.890
Besides, Nate let me grope her when she was braless,

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.370
<i>so I know I'm cool with firm ones, too! </i>

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:49.600
<i>It's all good!</i>

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.060
You're horrible! Absolutely horrible!

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:57.070
Ha, ha, ha! Bluntly put, you're horrible.

00:11:57.350 --> 00:12:00.780
I conclude that we are inversely parallel.

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:03.070
We are parallel.

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:09.020
Asama Shrine

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:07.020
<i>Therefore I say: Please leave.</i>

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:09.040
Aoi, don't give up!

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.560
<i>What she really wants is...</i>

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:13.230
<i>Don't worry, Seijun.</i>

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:13.790
Huh?

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:15.670
<i>I noticed as well.</i>

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:18.050
<i>This is a battle of debate.</i>

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:21.620
Since we're parallel, I'll say this:

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:24.220
I will take you back with me.

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:31.230
We're parallel, therefore I say:
We cannot reach an agreement.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:37.480
We're parallel, so I say:
I know we can reach an agreement.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:43.950
We're parallel, therefore I say:
You can't do anything, can you?

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:50.290
We're parallel, so I say:
I think I can do something for you.

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:55.620
We're parallel, therefore I say:
I want to die.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:13:00.610
We're parallel, so I say:
I want you to live.

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:03.470
I do not have a human life.

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:07.030
I know that you have a human soul.

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:09.470
Automated dolls do not have emotions.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:12.300
I will return your emotions to you.

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:13.730
It is all meaningless.

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:16.650
I don't think anything about you is meaningless.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:19.360
Automated dolls have perfect judgment.

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:22.610
I don't think your judgment is perfect.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:26.440
We are parallel, therefore I say:

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:30.870
I do not want to hear your responses.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:34.370
You don't wanna hear my responses?

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:38.910
But see, in the end,
that makes us inversely parallel.

00:13:38.910 --> 00:13:44.220
So I say: I want to hear your
response from a parallel standpoint.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:47.090
Judge,

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:48.530
very well.

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:50.190
Since we are parallel,

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:53.600
I am bound to respond to everything you have said.

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:56.830
I see. So it's all parallel.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:14:01.070
So I say:
Your judgment is probably perfect.

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:08.690
We're parallel, therefore I say:
I am certain that I am mistaken.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:11.520
Why?

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:13.770
How could an automatic doll be wrong when they

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:14.950
always make the best choices?

00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:22.570
Rarely Metabolisable
Ohiroshiki

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:19.960
The best choice doesn't necessarily
equal what she actually wants.

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:22.590
Perhaps she was waiting...

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:25.580
...for someone to make her give up.

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:28.900
We're parallel, so I say:

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:32.300
You think everything about you is meaningless.

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:35.970
We're parallel, therefore I say:

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:39.310
I don't want to think anything about me is meaningless.

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:45.280
We're parallel, so I say:
Don't you have any emotions?

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:51.180
We're parallel, therefore I say:
I believe I have emotions.

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:57.090
We're parallel, so I say:
Don't you have a human life?

00:14:57.090 --> 00:15:03.340
We're parallel, therefore I say:
I have a human soul.

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:05.930
You probably want to die.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:08.080
I want to live.

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:11.170
You think I can't do anything, don't you?

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:13.770
There's something you can do.

00:15:14.090 --> 00:15:16.590
We'll never reach an agreement.

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:20.060
We're parallel, therefore I say:

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:24.030
I know where we can reach an agreement.

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:26.200
And where is that, Horizon?

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:31.040
Since we're parallel,
where could we possibly intersect?

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:36.250
Judge, where all parallel lines meet.

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:39.560
Where conflicting ideals are reconciled.

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:40.870
It is...

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:47.310
...above the horizon.

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:51.700
Rarely Metabolisable
Ohiroshiki

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:55.470
Horizon, you don't want to go
above the horizon, do you?

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:57.720
No, I want to go.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:15:59.730
Don't want me to take you?

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:02.230
No, please take me.

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.730
But I can't do anything.

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:08.230
No, you can do any and everything.

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:10.740
And I can't fondle your boobies, can I?

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:13.490
Huh? What was that?

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:15.920
Crap! You answered like normal!

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:17.240
<i>Go die.</i>

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.780
Butt out!

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:22.040
Serving as sovereign is the best option.

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:27.520
However, I would prefer to work
as a saleslady in that café.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.090
Which would you have me do?

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.770
Jeez, you can do both!

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:36.300
I'm Student Council President and Chancellor,
but I still goof off.

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:37.620
Judge.

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:42.490
Honestly, I would like to
consider that the best option.

00:16:42.490 --> 00:16:44.200
Same here, Horizon.

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:46.060
This wall's in the way, huh?

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:49.150
We can't make out with it here.

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:50.610
You're the worst.

00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:52.360
You mean the best!

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:54.370
How do you break it?

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:56.060
Don't waste your time.

00:16:56.060 --> 00:16:56.810
Huh?

00:16:56.810 --> 00:16:59.990
No one has touched it and come back alive.

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:03.070
Hey, guys! Stop that old fart.

00:17:03.070 --> 00:17:05.040
He's hampering my flirt time with Horizon.

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:06.540
You bastard!

00:17:10.950 --> 00:17:12.020
What was that...?

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:14.890
I severed it with Slicing Dragonfly.

00:17:15.890 --> 00:17:18.030
I am Musashi Ariadust Academy's temporary

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:20.510
Vice Chancellor, Futayo Honda.

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:24.430
My sovereign, Horizon Ariadust,

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:28.850
wishes to survive,
so I have come to her aid.

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:30.990
Get it back!

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:34.650
Don't let the Far East
take the power of a Deadly Sin!

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:38.030
Protect the Chancellor!

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:43.410
Such recklessness...

00:17:44.060 --> 00:17:47.320
Hasn't the Far East endured for the past 160 years?

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:50.130
A dozen seconds more is nothing!

00:17:50.430 --> 00:17:52.690
Then I want a face off!

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:56.260
I want a showdown with Musashi's Chancellor!

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:59.850
First you must defeat me, his Vice Chancellor.

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:04.480
Fighting for some-odd seconds more is nothing for me.

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:07.140
Hey, ancient Pope!

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:10.010
I'm finishing up here, so just hang tight.

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:11.950
I have an engagement here first.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.350
Unexpected erotic moment!

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:24.510
Isn't this...?

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:26.430
Is this when Horizon died?

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:28.320
Horizon?

00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:31.770
I would have been fine if someone
touched it by themselves,

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:34.650
but I believe you were touching my breast.

00:18:34.650 --> 00:18:36.800
Is it seriously that simple?

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:37.800
That's...

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:42.320
My sister was out that day.

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:46.270
Horizon made breakfast for me since I slept in.

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:51.530
She was a rotten cook, so I said it was nasty.

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:54.360
Wasn't that only natural?

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:59.940
But Horizon started crying and ran off.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:21.970
Your hand...

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:25.930
This really is my sin.

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:29.570
You wouldn't have died if I didn't chase after you.

00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:32.550
I could have saved you if I was stronger.

00:19:33.390 --> 00:19:36.690
I really am an idiot incapable of doing anything.

00:19:37.120 --> 00:19:40.740
But seeing this, there was no saving you.

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:43.370
You sound as if this doesn't concern you.

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:45.560
What color do you like?

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:46.810
Black and white.

00:19:46.810 --> 00:19:49.330
Dude, you really are her!

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:53.980
So? How do you intend to deny this?

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:55.750
Horizon!

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:59.510
We are beginning to disintegrate.

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:01.620
What will you do?

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:07.520
Is disappearing together
where we meet above the horizon?

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:10.890
I will ask you bluntly.

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:14.520
Why did you fall in love with the present me?

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:20.280
I was surprised when I heard
that you practice making breakfast.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:25.530
I have no memories, so overlapping it
with this is meaningless.

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:27.830
But it made me think...

00:20:28.360 --> 00:20:31.660
You're the type of girl who wants to work hard

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:33.580
to make breakfast for someone.

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:38.800
I want to be with you and be
your number one guy, Horizon.

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:40.820
Is that right?

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:45.640
Then why did the past you
fall in love with the past Horizon?

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:47.210
Well...

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:51.180
If the reason is equal to why you want me now,

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:55.520
you're a strong partner capable of denying

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:57.690
the past Horizon via parallelism.

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:02.440
B-but the past Horizon ran from me.

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:05.410
The past Horizon did not run from you.

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:07.680
She was trying to hide.

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:08.370
Why?

00:21:08.820 --> 00:21:10.510
It is simple.

00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:13.040
To avoid becoming indebted to you

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:15.620
so you could stand as equal partners,

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:20.130
I gather that she wanted to greet you with a smile.

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:23.130
We are parallel.

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:28.140
I am certain that when you tried to save
the past Horizon, you yelled...

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:29.750
"I'm on my way!"

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:32.140
And then you said,

00:21:32.340 --> 00:21:34.890
"Stay back!" I believe.

00:21:36.460 --> 00:21:37.400
I...

00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:39.760
We are parallel.

00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:42.860
I told you not to come because we are parallel.

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:46.540
In that case, what should you say

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:49.000
so that we can go above the horizon?

00:21:56.300 --> 00:22:00.170
Horizon, I will say this to deny my past sin.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:02.880
If I can't save you by myself...

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:04.630
It's dangerous over there.

00:22:05.020 --> 00:22:09.390
I'm gonna go save you, but I want you
to come to me, Horizon.

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:50.260
Sora ni nozomu you ni

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:50.260
Our voyage across the real world

00:22:50.540 --> 00:22:57.270
Koukai suru genjitsu sekai no tabi

00:22:50.540 --> 00:22:57.270
Is like navigating straight for the sky

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:01.610
Nani mo mottenai kedo

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:01.610
I may not have anything

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.720
Kokoro no naka

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.720
But I have a dream

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:08.950
Kagayaita yume ga aru yo

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:08.950
That's shone brightly in my heart

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.790
Mada kikoenai

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.790
I still haven't heard

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:15.280
Kimi no hontou no mune no koe

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:15.280
The voice spoken from your heart

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:20.200
Shiritain da — sugao wo misete yo

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:20.200
Let me in — show me the real you

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:23.790
Barabara ni chirabatta

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:23.790
We'll bury the void

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:26.890
Ikutsu mo no piisu wo

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:26.890
As we find all of the pieces

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:29.560
Hitotsu zutsu sagashite

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:29.560
That have gotten scattered around

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.720
Kuuhaku wo umete iku no sa

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.720
One piece at a time

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:37.540
Ubawareta kimi no egao

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:37.540
Your smile has been stolen

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:41.210
Tori modosu tame ni hashiru yo

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:41.210
But I will race to get it back

00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:47.150
Boku wa hikari sasu michi wo

00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:47.150
As I run down the shining path

00:24:07.150 --> 00:24:10.990
Next Episode
Those Lined Up Above the Horizon
